I'm trying to write a function that would use Greek letters in a title and legend on a plot.  It seems to only way I can use Greek letters is by using the guiPlot( ) rather than just plot( ).  My problem is that I want to define the data as part of the function and I cannot figure out how to create a permanent data frame (one that would show up in Object Explorer) as part of a function.  It seems that guiPlot will only recognize existing data frames, not a temporary one that a function typically creates.

I've tried write.table( ) but to no avail.  I've also tried a number of things to insert Greek letters with the simple plot( ) function.

Basically my function would be something like

my.plot <- function(data.frame)

