Dear all,

Using the command line (and avoiding using "GuiCreate"), how can I specify a 
vector of characters to be used for x axis tick labels in a 2D scatterplot?

Suppose, I´d like to plot a variable, x, against another, y, e.g.

x_c(1,3,5,7,9)
y_c(2,4,6,8,10)

such that the x axis tick labels are c("A","B","C","D",""E") rather than 
1,3,5,7,9.

I´m thinking of a command which can be used within the "plot" command, e.g.
plot(x,y,ticklabels=c("A".....))

Thanks for your help!

Christoph.

