Since a factor (as distinct from an ordered factor) has no ordering, how
can your `I thought' possibly be correct?

Both tree and rpart divide the levels of an unordered factor into two 
non-empty groups.  As far as I recall rpart splits an ordered factor on 
its ordering but tree treats it as if unordered  But you can always 
replace an ordered factor by the codes in tree.

