If some one out there would like a simple extension of theMAD
principle for robust covariance estimation then here it is.
It is very nice because it extends MAD to a corr. coef and to
covariance and the relationship between MAD covariance and MAD standard 
deviation estimation
is the similar to the usual cov function and variance.  It would be easy for 
anyone to write
their own S+ program just using the definition.  If you do do this
please refer to my work.  See WEB site:
www. math.umt.edu/gideon
Then go to paper #1 (not #1a) and see the PDF file.  It
is section number 4 and in particular 4.2.
MAD correlation has just been studied in a  spatial statistics
study simulation and it does better than the existing spatial
robust method.
Please don't take my word for it, try it out.
Rudy Gideon, University of Montana

